<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
                           xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                           revision="1.0"
                           schemaVersion="1.0"
                           xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>ModernWork Elevate</displayName>
  <description>Machine-wide settings for ModernWork Elevate.</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_ModernWorkElevate_1_2">ModernWork Elevate 1.2 or later on Windows 11 25H2 or later</string>
      <string id="Cat_ModernWorkElevate">ModernWork Elevate</string>

      <string id="Tenants">Pre-configured tenants and App Registrations</string>
      <string id="Tenants_Help">Pre-configures the tenants users of this device can sign in to.

Value name: the tenant (directory) ID, a GUID.
Value: the application (client) ID of the App Registration to use in that tenant, optionally followed by ;Label and ;Cloud.

Examples:
  Value name 11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555, value aaaaaaaa-bbbb-cccc-dddd-eeeeeeeeeeee
  Value name 11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555, value aaaaaaaa-bbbb-cccc-dddd-eeeeeeeeeeee;Contoso;Global

Cloud is Global (default) or China. An entry here replaces a tenant entry the user configured for the same tenant. Invalid entries are ignored and logged.

If enabled: the listed tenants are available to every user; users may add further tenants unless "Lock the tenant list" is enabled.
If disabled or not configured: users configure their tenants themselves.</string>

      <string id="LockTenants">Lock the tenant list</string>
      <string id="LockTenants_Help">If enabled, only the tenants from "Pre-configured tenants and App Registrations" are available. Tenants the user configured are ignored, and users cannot add, change or remove tenants.

If disabled or not configured, users can add tenants in addition to the pre-configured ones.</string>


    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="Tenants">
        <listBox refId="TenantsList">Tenants (value name = tenant ID, value = client ID[;label[;cloud]]):</listBox>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
